I mean, she is so, so wonderful on the pit.
我是说，她在《镀金时代》里的表现实在是太、太棒了。

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:21.230
I'm really just so floored by her performance.
她的表演真的让我惊艳不已。

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:22.470
Thanks, Josh.
谢谢你，乔什。

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:26.189
You know, I mean, first of all, it doesn't even have to be as an actor.
你知道的，首先，甚至都不必非是以演员的身份。

00:04:26.189 --> 00:04:36.750
But any person who praises your kid for anything is just, it makes the parent feel like, okay, I'm good.
任何因为任何事情而夸奖你孩子的人，都会让身为人父母的觉得，好吧，我做得不错。

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:37.750
I can walk away.
我可以放心了。

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:40.509
It was worth it to come on here today.
今天来这里一趟太值得了。

00:04:40.509 --> 00:04:50.629
So when Malcolm went off the air, did you have that feeling that an actor, I was told years ago by a manager, all actors believe two things at one any given time.
所以当《马尔科姆》停播时，你有没有那种感觉——几年前一个经纪人跟我说过，所有演员在任何特定时刻都深信两件事：第一，我的经纪人对我还不够努力；第二，我目前的工作将是我的最后一份工作。

00:04:50.629 --> 00:04:52.990
One, my reps aren't working hard enough for me.
（接上条）第二，我目前的工作将是我的最后一份工作。

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:55.664
two, the job I currently have will be my last.
（接上条）第二，我目前的工作将是我的最后一份工作。

00:04:55.664 --> 00:04:59.966
Were you in that feeling of like, okay, this great run on this show ended?
当时你是否有那种感觉，比如“好吧，这部剧里这段伟大的经历结束了”？你是否突然又回到了“我需要找份工作”的状态？

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:02.990
Were you suddenly back in like, I need to get a job?
不，不，不，我，嗯……当我25岁的时候，我搬到了纽约市去演肥皂剧。

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:13.360
No, no, no, I, um, it wasn't when I was 25 years old, I moved to New York City to do a soap opera.
是的。

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:14.500
Yeah.
虽然该剧的质量或该媒介中的任何节目都不是最高标准，因为它们的制作节奏实在太快了。

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:23.654
And while the quality of the show or any of those shows in that medium, we're not of the highest standard because they just went so fast.
一旦你拍完，就把它扔掉，拍下一集，再把那个扔掉，拍下一集，再扔掉。

00:05:23.654 --> 00:05:31.205
As soon as you're done, you throw it away, you got the next one, throw that away, do the next one, throw it away.
（接上条）拍下一集，再把那个扔掉，拍下一集，再扔掉。

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:33.328
It's such a churn.
这种工作流就像是一台永动机。

00:05:33.328 --> 00:05:34.894
Yeah, I saw Tootsie.
对，我看过《窈窕淑男》。

00:05:34.894 --> 00:05:35.442
I know.
我知道。

00:05:35.442 --> 00:05:36.694
You saw Tootsie.
你看过《窈窕淑男》。

00:05:36.694 --> 00:05:37.946
Yeah, I know it.
是的，我知道。

00:05:37.946 --> 00:05:46.399
But it was such a churn and such a chore to be able to look at that work and try to find moments of honesty.
但这真是一项流水线似的工作，要在那种工作中审视自己的表演并试图找到真诚的时刻，简直是一种折磨。

00:05:46.399 --> 00:05:50.399
You can't find extended moments because it just doesn't know time.
你无法找到持久的真诚时刻，因为根本没有那个时间。

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:53.199
You're focused on learning those lines and that's gone.
你的注意力都集中在背台词上，拍完就过去了。

00:05:54.000 --> 00:06:00.480
But at that time in 1983, I realized that I crossed a threshold.
但在1983年的那个时候，我意识到我跨过了一个门槛。

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:05.519
There was something within me that said, oh, I can do this.
我内心里有一种声音在说，哦，我能做到。

00:06:05.519 --> 00:06:06.480
I belong here.
我属于这里。

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:09.360
I feel confident that I'm in.
我确信我入选了。

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:14.639
I am now going to make a living as an actor exclusively for the rest of my life.
我从今以后要靠当演员来维持生计，余生只做这一行。

00:06:14.639 --> 00:06:16.298
And that's what happened.
事实也确实如此。

00:06:16.298 --> 00:06:17.559
It was that moment.
就是那一刻。

00:06:17.559 --> 00:06:28.771
So no, I I don't have that feeling of I'll never work again I I don't it just changed in me at that time It's an expression that has an asterisk by it and at the bottom.
所以，不，我不会有那种“我再也找不到工作了”的感觉，我不会，那种感觉当时就在我心里改变了，这是一个后面带星号的表述，在底部。

00:06:28.771 --> 00:06:35.008
It says accept to Brian Cranston Did you feel that way when your show ended did you freak out?
上面写着，除了布莱恩·克兰斯顿。你的节目结束时你有那种感觉吗？你当时慌了吗？

00:06:35.008 --> 00:06:42.240
No, I didn't feel that way when the show ended I definitely felt like I have some rethinking of things to do.
不，节目结束时我没有那种感觉，我绝对觉得我有些事情需要重新思考。

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:56.720
And I have to be careful and judicious about what I do when I do it, how I'm gonna, and I had a broader idea of myself as a maker of things that I wasn't only about acting, but I know what you mean.
而且我必须谨慎、明智地对待我所做的事情、何时去做、我将如何去做，我对自己的看法更广泛了，我不仅是一个演员，更是一个创造者，但我明白你的意思。

00:06:56.720 --> 00:07:01.160
I'm curious though, you were how old, like in your mid 20s around that time.
不过我很好奇，你当时多大，大概二十多岁的时候。

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:15.160
And there was just some internal shift where you said, I can do this and I'm gonna keep doing this and not, like I mean, I think it's a, I think in some ways success is a bit of a psychological game, you know, I mean, there's plenty of people.
当时内心发生了某种转变，你说，我能做到这一点，而且我会一直做下去，而不是，我的意思是，我认为，在某些方面，成功有点像是一场心理游戏，你知道的，我是说，有很多人。

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:25.399
I used to, I said this once that a lot of people have the talent for acting, but not everyone has the stomach, you know, that there's a lot of like, you got to take a lot of clocks on the chin and just stay in it.
我以前说过，我曾说过这样的话：很多人都有演戏的天赋，但并不是所有人都有那份韧劲，你知道的，就是你必须挨很多记闷棍，然后咬牙坚持下去。

00:07:25.399 --> 00:07:29.839
So you just have this essential kind of belief in yourself that never dimmed.
所以你只是对自我有着一种从未消减的根本信念。

00:07:29.839 --> 00:07:39.399
No, I mean, but that's not to say there aren't frustrating periods that you go through and your ebb and flow of a career.
不，我的意思是，但这并不是说你的职业生涯中不会经历令人沮丧的低谷期和起伏。

00:07:39.399 --> 00:07:50.319
But as I tell you, people who want to become actors or writers, directors, producers, whatever, I said, you've got to commit to the relationship of this.
但正如我告诉那些想成为演员、作家、导演、制片人或其它什么的人一样，我说，你必须全身心投入到与这行的关系中。

00:07:50.319 --> 00:07:55.759
You have to commit to it like you're committing to in your personal life, you know?
你必须像对待个人生活中的承诺一样去承诺它，你知道吗？

00:07:55.759 --> 00:07:59.279
If you will not make it, if you say, I'm gonna give it to you, we won't hurt.
如果你只是说，我打算试试，那你就不会成功，我们不会受伤的。

00:07:59.279 --> 00:08:00.879
I'm gonna give it two years.
我打算给它两年时间。

00:08:00.879 --> 00:08:02.360
Right, it's like saying a marriage.
对，这就好像在谈论婚姻一样。

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:03.600
Like, I'm gonna give this two years.
就像，我打算把这桩婚姻维持两年。

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:11.259
And if I hit any rough spots in my marriage amount, it won't work if you're just dipping your toe into it.
如果我的婚姻遇到任何坎坷，如果你只是浅尝辄止，那是行不通的。

00:08:11.259 --> 00:08:14.379
So that's what I was committed to it.
所以这就是我所承诺的。

00:08:14.379 --> 00:08:20.259
I had a bunch of survival jobs before I was waiting tables or I loaded trucks.
在我成名前我做过很多维持生计的工作，我当过服务员，也搬过货。

00:08:20.259 --> 00:08:27.180
And every time I was at work, I would say one of these days, one day I'm getting closer and closer.
每次我在工作时，我都会对自己说，总有一天，总有一天我会越来越近。

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:32.019
One day I'll be able to say I work exclusively as an actor.
总有一天，我能说我专职当演员了。

00:08:32.019 --> 00:08:47.580
And I gotta say, that was my happiest moment to my, to this day, that also feels like my most accomplished moment that when I crossed over and I said, oh my God, this, I can do this and I, I belong here.
我必须得说，那是我至今为止最快乐的时刻，这也感觉是我最有成就感的时刻，当我跨过那道门槛，我说，哦天哪，这个，我能做到，而且我，我属于这里。

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:49.279
I'll tell you a story.
我给你讲个故事。

