00:17:00.789 --> 00:17:01.789
So that was, that was fun.
所以这确实很有趣。

00:17:01.789 --> 00:17:04.670
It's also, it's also like, um, consequentialist free bad behavior.
而且这也是一种……不用承担后果的恶劣行为。

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:10.549
Like you get to really exercise, like your shadow gets to come out and play and it's like you're beloved for it.
就像你可以彻底释放，让你的阴暗面出来玩耍，而且人们还因此而喜爱你。

00:17:10.549 --> 00:17:11.829
You know, you're really, right.
你知道的，确实如此，对吧。

00:17:11.829 --> 00:17:21.990
I also, I was watching the episode again, Brian, and I had this feeling for both of us, but especially for you, I can't believe this is our adult job.
另外，布赖恩，我再次看这集的时候，我有一种感觉，对我们两个来说，尤其是对你，我简直不敢相信这是我们成年后的工作。

00:17:21.990 --> 00:17:29.069
I can't believe this is how he is feeding his family, like, through doing this.
我简直不敢相信他竟然是靠做这个来养家糊口。

00:17:29.069 --> 00:17:31.109
When he's screaming at the child with the ice cream.
当他对拿着冰淇淋的小孩大喊大叫的时候。

00:17:31.109 --> 00:17:34.069
Yeah, he's screaming at a child with an ice cream cone.
对，他对一个拿着冰淇淋甜筒的小孩大喊大叫。

00:17:34.069 --> 00:17:37.190
Like, this is how he's gonna pay for things.
就像，他居然靠这个来付账单。

00:17:37.190 --> 00:17:38.630
Like, it's unbelievable.
简直难以置信。

00:17:38.630 --> 00:17:39.470
Isn't it?
不是吗？

00:17:39.470 --> 00:17:41.509
I wish that for all of us.
我希望我们所有人都能这样。

00:17:41.509 --> 00:17:46.509
I am never without that sense of what good fortune we've had.
我无时无刻不为我们拥有这样的好运而感恩。

00:17:46.509 --> 00:17:50.990
and to be able to just say, this is what we do for a living.
能够直言不讳地说，这就是我们谋生的手段。

00:17:50.990 --> 00:18:07.349
It can be hard, you know, when you're on a sound stage every day, we've talked about this in the podcast, you forget, you know, it's such a cocooned kind of environment, you forget that it's being beamed out to all over the world, you know, and that actually, sometimes you can think, oh, I should be in the Peace Corps.
你知道的，这有时也会很艰难，当你每天都待在摄影棚里时，我们在这个播客里也讨论过，你会忘记——这是一种非常封闭的环境——你会忘记它正在向全世界播出，你知道的，有时候你可能会想，哦，我应该去和平队。

00:18:07.349 --> 00:18:12.470
I should be doing something in a nonprofit or some sort of altruistic kind of impulse thing.
我应该去做一些非营利组织的工作，或者某种带有某种利他主义冲动的事情。

00:18:12.470 --> 00:18:21.869
And then you think, no, people come up to you and they have those jobs, or they have gone through hard times and they're like, your show was the source of lightness and laughter in my life.
然后你会想，不，人们会走到你面前，他们从事着那些工作，或者他们经历过艰难的时期，他们会说：你们的剧给我的人生带来了光明和欢笑。

00:18:21.869 --> 00:18:23.950
Like you realize it's a real public service.
这时你会意识到，这是一项真正的公共服务。

00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:24.450
Exactly.
没错。

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:27.809
To make people laugh, to divert, to entertain, you know.
逗人笑，解闷，娱乐大众，你知道的。

00:18:27.789 --> 00:18:43.740
And did you have that feeling always or was it your experience on the show and hearing those comments from the public that you start to say, oh, I guess simple entertainment has tremendous value to people.
你一直都有这种感觉，还是说因为你在剧中的经历以及听到公众的这些评价，你才开始觉得，哦，原来单纯的娱乐对人们有着巨大的价值？

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:50.900
Well, I think I always had a sense of it, but I have the largest sample size from how I met your mother fans, just because I did more of that than anything else.
嗯，我想我一直都有这种感觉，但我从《老爸老妈浪漫史》的粉丝那里得到了最大样本量的反馈，因为我拍那个的时间比其他任何作品都多。

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:52.859
So I hear from more of those people.
所以我听到更多这样的人的反馈。

00:18:52.859 --> 00:19:01.440
And one of the things we're interrogating in this show is what is that kind of special soul medicine that how I met your mother seems to have beyond just a comedy.
我们在剧中探讨的一点是，除了单纯的喜剧之外，《老爸老妈浪漫史》似乎还具有那种特殊的灵魂药剂究竟是什么。

00:19:01.440 --> 00:19:11.099
A lot of shows can make you laugh, but there was this additional element of that it felt like a friend to people, that it was a comforting show through their tough times.
很多剧都能让你发笑，但它还有一个额外的元素，那就是它感觉像是人们的朋友，在他们艰难的时刻给予他们慰藉。

00:19:11.099 --> 00:19:15.980
And we've heard from autistic people who said, this taught me social cues.
我们听到过自闭症患者说，这部剧教会了我社交线索。

00:19:15.980 --> 00:19:20.059
Like this taught me how to be in the world in a different way.
就像这部剧教会了我如何以一种不同的方式融入世界。

00:19:20.059 --> 00:19:23.259
And that's the stuff that is particularly startling.
这些事情尤其让人震动。

00:19:23.259 --> 00:19:25.859
Like how to pick up women from Barney?
比如从巴尼那里学怎么泡妞吗？

00:19:25.859 --> 00:19:27.420
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
行，行，行。

00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:30.059
How not to be a boss from Ham and Brothers?
如何不做《马尔柯姆的一家》里那样的老板？

00:19:30.059 --> 00:19:31.059
We did it.
我们做到了。

00:19:31.059 --> 00:19:32.059
We did have a question.
我们确实有个问题。

00:19:32.059 --> 00:19:33.059
Craig and I were talking about this.
克雷格和我正在讨论这个。

00:19:33.059 --> 00:19:45.259
I don't know if this was your first horrible boss, but it's not your last because your character of the studio is also probably in your your lineage of these kind of insane bosses.
我不知道这算不算你的第一个可怕老板，但绝对不会是最后一个，因为你演艺生涯中遇到的角色里，大概也有一脉这种疯狂的老板。

00:19:45.259 --> 00:19:46.448
Yes, it is funny.
对，这挺有意思的。

00:19:46.448 --> 00:19:52.601
You're back in the insane boss world a little bit, although it's a very different twist.
你又稍微回到了疯狂老板的世界，尽管这次有很不一样的转折。

00:19:52.601 --> 00:19:55.677
That show is great and you were great on it.
那部剧很棒，你在里面的表现也非常好。

00:19:55.677 --> 00:20:01.900
That's is it fun getting to be an unhinged ego maniac boss with sort of a different spin?
能演一个精神错乱、利己主义、带点不同风格的老板，这很有趣吗？

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:03.089
It's so much fun.
太有趣了。

00:20:03.089 --> 00:20:11.758
Of course, it's done in that single camera style with kind of that one or with stitching going on with the with some things.
当然，它是用单机位风格拍摄的，带有那种或者说带有一些镜头衔接的处理。

00:20:11.758 --> 00:20:12.877
But so much fun.
但真的非常有趣。

00:20:12.877 --> 00:20:18.610
And again, once again, like, you guys who created the show, the writing was there.
而且，再次说明，像你们这些创作这部剧的人，剧本真的很到位。

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:22.316
If the writing's not present, it's not going to work.
如果剧本不行，那就演不出效果。

00:20:22.316 --> 00:20:27.980
And, you know, Seth Rogen and Evan Goldberg, they're really funny, funny writers.
而且，你知道的，塞斯·罗根和埃文·戈德堡，他们真的是非常幽默的编剧。

00:20:27.980 --> 00:20:31.099
And they get it, so it was fun to do.
他们懂这个，所以演起来很有趣。

00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:38.859
Do you get, I'm just curious, this is just for me, do you get nervous during one or is like in a different way or do you just get used to that's the way you're shooting.
我只是好奇，纯粹为了我自己，你在演一镜到底或者不同风格的时候会紧张吗，还是说你已经习惯了那种拍摄方式？

00:20:38.859 --> 00:20:41.980
I mean it's more like theater in a way like you just you got to do the whole thing.
我的意思是，某种程度上它更像戏剧，你必须把整段全演下来。

00:20:43.099 --> 00:20:52.547
I think what my daughter is going through is probably the hardest work to have right now as she plays a doctor on the bit.
我觉得我女儿现在经历的可能是最难应付的工作，因为她在戏里演一个医生。

00:20:52.547 --> 00:21:07.259
They have the six or seven syllable words medical terminology right that they're whipping to someone whipping back to you, go, and blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah.
她们有六、七个音节的医学专业术语，需要连珠炮似地甩给别人，别人又连珠炮似地甩回给你，就是“巴拉巴拉巴拉”这一套。

00:21:07.259 --> 00:21:12.420
And if you didn't get it, we got to do it over and you're thinking, oh, my god, what's the words of...
如果你没接住，我们就得重来，然后你在想，天哪，那些词到底是……

00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:13.880
Yeah, this is not English.
对，这不是英语。

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:15.400
This is a different language.
这是另一门语言。

00:21:15.400 --> 00:21:19.039
It is learning a different language.
这确实是在学一门不同的语言。

00:21:19.039 --> 00:21:22.539
So that's the tough part.
所以这才是最难的部分。

00:21:22.539 --> 00:21:25.319
Can I ask, what is the...
我能问一下，那个……

00:21:25.319 --> 00:21:32.279
My father had his own negotiation with kind of accepting that his son was not going to be a lawyer.
我父亲曾经历过一番内心的挣扎，才最终接受他儿子不会成为一名律师。

00:21:32.279 --> 00:21:35.279
He was going to be an actor, and now is his own process.
他要当演员，如今这也是他自己的一段心路历程。

00:21:35.279 --> 00:21:38.079
But your daughter went into your line of work.
但你的女儿走上了你这一行。

00:21:38.079 --> 00:21:39.079
What was that like?
那是一种什么体验？

00:21:39.079 --> 00:21:44.440
I mean, I imagine there must be untold amounts of pride and joy now.
我的意思是，我想现在肯定有说不清的骄傲和喜悦吧。

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:48.440
But were you nervous about, did you try to prepare her?
但你当时会感到紧张吗？你有没有试着去开导她？

00:21:48.440 --> 00:21:52.430
I'm just curious how much ever much you want to share about that.
我只是好奇，你想分享多少都可以。

00:21:52.430 --> 00:21:56.750
Well, parents are always teaching their children.
嗯，父母总是在教育孩子。

00:21:56.750 --> 00:22:04.349
In the best case scenario, hopefully, it's how to behave, how to be a good person, a kind person, a respectful person.
在最好的情况下，希望是教他们如何做人，如何做一个好人、善良的人、懂得尊重的人。

00:22:04.349 --> 00:22:14.390
In some cases, in my case, in many times, when I was a child, it was, oh, my parents did that, so that didn't work, so I'm gonna do this.
但在某些情况下，就我而言，很多时候当我还是个孩子的时候，就会想：“哦，我父母那样做过，结果行不通，所以我得这么做。”

00:22:14.390 --> 00:22:18.990
You know, but both of my parents were actors.
你知道的，但我的父母都是演员。

00:22:18.990 --> 00:22:19.990
Oh, I didn't know that.
哦，我不知道这件事。

00:22:19.990 --> 00:22:33.799
Yeah, they met on a show in 1951 called Life with Elizabeth starring Betty White, and they played her next-door neighbor.
对，他们1951年在一档名为《与伊丽莎白同行》的节目中相遇，该剧由贝蒂·怀特主演，他们在剧中演她的邻居。

00:22:33.799 --> 00:22:42.039
They were a married couple next to her, they got married, they started having kids, and so they were actors as well.
他们演她隔壁的一对已婚夫妇，后来他们结婚了，开始生孩子，所以他们也是演员。

00:22:42.039 --> 00:22:43.039
Okay.
原来如此。

00:22:43.039 --> 00:22:59.410
about it, guys, it is probably the most common matriculation in the world to go from school to your life's work in your family business.
说实话，伙计们，从学校毕业直接进入家族企业从事终身事业，这可能是世界上最普遍的传承方式了。

00:22:59.410 --> 00:23:05.049
There are probably more people around the world who just follow up if you're a farmer, you're a farmer.
世界上可能有更多的人只是顺理成章地继承父业，如果你是个农民，你就是个农民。

00:23:05.049 --> 00:23:11.049
If you're a dry cleaner, you inherit, you're just like, whatever your paint houses you do, whatever you do.
如果你家开干洗店，你就会继承它，或者不管你是粉刷房屋还是做什么，反正就是子承父业。

00:23:11.049 --> 00:23:18.369
When you think about it in those terms, it's like, oh, of course she's, she's got, she's exposed to what it's like to be an actor.
如果从这个角度去想，就会觉得：“哦，当然了，她从小就耳濡目染演员的生活是什么样的。”

00:23:18.369 --> 00:23:22.650
Well, she was on, she was on sets with you from, from the time she can remember, right?
对啊，她从记事起就经常去片场探你的班，对吧？

00:23:22.650 --> 00:23:23.970
Yeah, she was, she would come in.
对，她会来。

00:23:23.970 --> 00:23:26.089
It was a very normal part of her life.
这是她生活中非常正常的一部分。

00:23:26.089 --> 00:23:27.089
But right.
不过话说回来。

00:23:27.089 --> 00:23:39.539
She also knew that, you know, I wasn't, I was 41 or 40, 41 when I did the pilot for Malcolm at the Battle, which was my first series that stuck.
她也很清楚，你知道的，我拍《马尔柯姆的一家》试播集时已经41岁了，40、41岁左右，那是我的第一部得以延续下去的剧集。

00:23:39.539 --> 00:23:41.799
I had done other series before.
我之前也拍过其他剧集。

00:23:41.799 --> 00:23:42.640
Right.
没错。

00:23:42.640 --> 00:23:46.400
Four episodes, six episodes, gone, gone, gone, gone.
四集、六集，然后就被砍了、砍了、砍了、砍了。

00:23:46.400 --> 00:23:48.119
It's like the life of an actor, you know?
这就是演员的生活，你知道吗？

00:23:48.119 --> 00:23:49.039
You're like, yeah.
你会觉得，唉，就是这样。

00:23:49.039 --> 00:23:57.240
And so my wife and I and our daughter, we had this little house in the valley and we were very adorable, very middle class.
所以我和我妻子还有女儿，我们在山谷区有一栋小房子，过着非常可爱、非常中产阶级的生活。

00:23:57.240 --> 00:24:01.559
We would work and we'd save that money because we didn't know when we were gonna work again.
我们会去工作，然后把钱存起来，因为我们不知道什么时候才能再接到工作。

00:24:01.559 --> 00:24:04.759
It was just like, okay, we got this, it's going.
当时的心态就是，好吧，我们有这个，日子在继续。

00:24:04.759 --> 00:24:07.839
And is it true, you also met your wife doing a show, isn't that right?
这是真的吗？你也是通过拍戏认识你妻子的，对吧？

00:24:07.839 --> 00:24:08.680
Yeah.
对。

00:24:08.680 --> 00:24:09.680
Yeah.
没错。

00:24:09.680 --> 00:24:13.000
So there's another in the family line.
所以家族里又多了一对同行。

00:24:13.000 --> 00:24:14.000
How I met your mother?
《老爸老妈浪漫史》？

00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:15.000
Yeah.
对。

00:24:15.000 --> 00:24:16.000
That's basically that.
差不多就是那样。

00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:23.559
38 or 39 years ago now, I met her on an episode.
现在算来，那是38或39年前了，我在一集节目里遇到了她。

00:24:23.559 --> 00:24:27.680
We were both guest stars on an episode of a show called Air Wolf.
我们俩都是一部叫《飞狼》的剧集某一集里的客串演员。

00:24:27.680 --> 00:24:28.680
Oh, sure.
哦，当然。

00:24:28.680 --> 00:24:29.680
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

00:24:29.680 --> 00:24:30.680
Do you know the issue?
你知道那部剧吗？

00:24:30.680 --> 00:24:31.680
Oh, I remember it.
哦，我记得。

00:24:31.680 --> 00:24:32.680
Was the helicopter?
就是有直升机那部？

00:24:32.680 --> 00:24:33.680
Yeah.
对。

00:24:33.680 --> 00:24:34.680
Oh, yes.
哦，对的。

00:24:34.680 --> 00:24:35.680
Jan Michael Vincent.
简·迈克尔·文森特。

00:24:35.680 --> 00:24:36.680
Yeah.
对。

00:24:36.680 --> 00:24:37.680
Yeah.
对。

00:24:37.680 --> 00:24:41.519
so silly, because they're cardboard cutouts.
真是太傻了，因为角色都是纸片人。

00:24:41.519 --> 00:24:44.079
Bad guy, good guy.
坏人、好人。

00:24:44.079 --> 00:24:50.279
On Genu, victim, you know, it's like, and everyone plays that role, stays in their lane.
无辜受害者，你知道的，就像那样，每个人都扮演好自己的角色，各司其职。

00:24:50.279 --> 00:24:52.079
And it's like, oh, God, but.
然后就会觉得，哦天哪，但是……

00:24:52.079 --> 00:24:53.680
And it has to involve a helicopter.
而且剧情必须得有直升机参与。

00:24:53.680 --> 00:24:57.759
That was before you got into more nuanced work like Hammond, brothers, exactly.
那是你涉足像《马尔柯姆的一家》这种更有细致内涵的作品之前的事了，确实。

00:24:57.759 --> 00:25:00.119
But they can't all be that multifaceted, look, come on.
但也不可能个个角色都那么丰富多变，拜托。

00:25:00.119 --> 00:25:01.160
Settle team.
放轻松。

00:25:01.160 --> 00:25:02.000
It's not all goals.
总不能回回都是杰作。

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:03.200
It's my signature.
这可是我的标志性风格。

00:25:03.200 --> 00:25:04.039
Yeah.
对。

00:25:04.039 --> 00:25:05.039
Yeah.
对。

00:25:05.039 --> 00:25:18.279
So yeah, I always think about children of actors who become actors, there's this kind of like, oh, they had every door open, my theory is they might have a door open, but if they don't have the talent, they will not walk through it.
所以，是的，我经常想到演员的孩子也去当演员这种事，大家总会觉得：“哦，他们一路开绿灯。”但我的理论是，他们或许能得到一个机会，但如果没有天赋，他们是走不远这一行的。

00:25:18.279 --> 00:25:27.680
They just, the business is too tricky and it's too much of a high wire act that if you can't do it, you're not gonna stick around.
这行太诡谲了，就像走钢丝一样，如果你做不来，你就无法在这行立足。

00:25:27.680 --> 00:25:42.789
And Taylor is so independent that she, as of now, And as of now, she's like very resistant to even considering auditioning for something that I may be doing.
而泰勒非常独立，到目前为止，而且直到现在，她都非常抗拒去考虑试镜任何我可能参与的项目。

00:25:42.789 --> 00:25:43.789
She won't do it.
她绝对不肯。

00:25:43.789 --> 00:25:44.789
She doesn't want any...
她不想……

00:25:44.789 --> 00:25:45.990
Oh, interesting.
哦，有意思。

00:25:45.990 --> 00:25:46.990
She doesn't want to work with...
她不想跟……

00:25:46.990 --> 00:25:47.990
She doesn't want to work with dads?
她不想跟老爸合作？

00:25:47.990 --> 00:25:48.990
It's too weird and so much pressure.
这太奇怪了，而且压力太大了。

